1
00:07:03,529 --> 00:07:09,529
A boy's journey. A mother's love. Miles of burning city between them.

2
00:14:07,058 --> 00:14:13,058
Blitz is a war, drama, history film directed by Steve McQueen.

3
00:21:10,588 --> 00:21:16,588
In World War II London, nine-year-old George is evacuated to the
countryside by his mother, Rita, to escape the bombings.

4
00:28:14,117 --> 00:28:20,117
Defiant and determined to return to his family, George embarks on an
epic, perilous journey back home as Rita searches for him.

5
00:35:17,647 --> 00:35:23,647
George, played by Elliott Heffernan.

6
00:42:21,176 --> 00:42:27,176
Rita, played by Saoirse Ronan.

7
00:49:24,705 --> 00:49:30,705
Ife, played by Benjamin Clementine.

8
00:56:28,235 --> 00:56:34,235
Gerald, played by Paul Weller.

9
01:03:31,764 --> 01:03:37,764
Albert, played by Stephen Graham.

10
01:10:35,294 --> 01:10:41,294
Jack, played by Harris Dickinson.

11
01:17:38,823 --> 01:17:44,823
Blitz  is a 2024 historical war drama film about WWII
written, produced and directed by Steve McQueen.

12
01:24:42,352 --> 01:24:48,352
The film stars Saoirse Ronan and Elliott Heffernan (in his film debut), supported by Harris
Dickinson, Benjamin Clementine, Kathy Burke, Paul Weller, and Stephen Graham.

13
01:31:45,882 --> 01:31:51,882
Blitz had its world premiere as the opening film at the BFI London Film Festival on 9 October 2024, and was released in selected cinemas in
the United Kingdom and United States on 1 November 2024, followed by a streaming release on Apple TV+ on 22 November 2024.

14
01:38:49,411 --> 01:38:55,411
The film received generally positive reviews from critics.

15
01:45:52,941 --> 01:45:58,941
